  "@type": "Recipe",
  "name": "Takikomi Gohan",
  "text": "Takikomi Gohan\n\nPreparation time:\n\nCooking time:\n\nYield: 2\n\nEquipment\n\nRice cooker\n\nIngredients\n\n180ml rice (washed),\n\n180ml dashi stock,\n\n70g chicken breast (cut into small bite sizes pieces),\n\n20g carrot (cut into matchsticks),\n\n25g burdock root (cut into matchsticks and rinsed in cold water),\n\n30g shitaki mushrooms (sliced then halved),\n\n20g maitake mushrooms (torn and chopped into small bite sized pieces),\n\n1/2 aburaage (thin deep fried tofu cut into short fingers),\n\n5g ginger root (thinly shredded),\n\nMitsuba parsley,\n\n1 tsp soy sauce,\n\n1/2 tsp salt,\n\n1 tbsp sake,\n\n1/2 tbsp mirin.\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Put the rice in a rice cooker and add the dashi stock.\n\n2. Marinate the chicken in the soy sauce, Dali, mirin and salt.\n\n3. Add the carrot, burdock, mushrooms, aburaage and ginger to the chicken.\n\n4. Add the mixture on top of the rice.\n\n5. Start the rice cooker as for ordinary rice cooking.\n\n6. When cooked, mix through and serve garnished with mitsuba parsley.",
  "recipeYield": "2",
